issue_comments.body:
@NicolasGorga thanks for the review, you were right, the service-layer wiring was redundant. I've reverted `product-module-service.ts` (commit ca7a1b6f77), so the only remaining change in the module is the `.searchable()` modifier on the `variants` relation in `Product`. Free text search is now applied automatically by `MedusaInternalService.applyFreeTextSearchFilter`. The integration tests still pass.

Also addressed the changeset comment (removed `integration-tests-http`).

@medusa-os-bot opened #15239 to describe the v1→v2 SKU search regression and linked it from the PR description with `Closes #15239`.

Re: the bot's note about `.searchable()` on `variants` covering `sku`, `title`, `barcode`, `ean`, and `upc` — that breadth is intentional. Those are exactly the fields warehouse/retail workflows search by (SKU, barcode scanner output, EAN/UPC), and matching the v1 admin behaviour was the goal. Happy to scope it down to SKU only if the team prefers, but I'd argue the current behaviour is the more useful default.

